q 0.1 0.2 0.4 rg
BT /F2 14 Tf 54 736 Td (ABSTRACT) Tj ET
Q
q 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 54 718 Td (Managing commercial airline operations manually or through fragmented legacy spreadsheets is an increasingly) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 54 704.5 Td (intractable challenge for aviation enterprises, particularly as passenger volumes, flight route frequencies, aircraft cabin) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 54 691.0 Td (topologies, and baggage custody logistics expand. Information related to flight route schedules, aircraft seating) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 54 677.5 Td (arrangements, passenger reservations, passenger name records \(PNRs\), e-ticketing, airport check-in custody, excess) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 54 664.0 Td (baggage fee collection, and cancellations is often scattered across disconnected ledgers, leading to relational) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 54 650.5 Td (inconsistency, double-booking contention, revenue leakage, and severe retrieval latency.) Tj ET
Q
q 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 54 633.0 Td (This project, titled 'Design and Implementation of a Database Management System for Airline Reservation and Flight) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 54 619.5 Td (Operations Management System' \(ARFOM-DB\), addresses these industry-critical failure modes by engineering and) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 54 606.0 Td (implementing a centralized, ACID-compliant relational database management system that systematically unifies all) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 54 592.5 Td (flight operations and passenger booking data.) Tj ET
Q
q 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 54 575.0 Td (The system models ten interrelated entities - Airports, Aircraft, Routes, Flights, Seats, Passengers, Bookings, Tickets,) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 54 561.5 Td (Payments, Check-ins, Baggage, and Cancellations - using a strictly normalized 3NF schema implemented in MySQL) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 54 548.0 Td (and SQLite. Primary key, composite unique, and foreign key constraints enforce referential integrity across the entire) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 54 534.5 Td (operational lifecycle, guaranteeing that duplicate seat bookings on identical flight legs are rejected at the storage) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 54 521.0 Td (engine level.) Tj ET
Q
q 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 54 503.5 Td (A high-contrast web-based administrative and customer operations interface was developed using modern HTML5,) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 54 490.0 Td (CSS3, and JavaScript on the frontend, communicating directly with a lightweight Python backend server through) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 54 476.5 Td (RESTful JSON endpoints. The interface allows authorized station dispatchers and passengers to view, search, filter,) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 54 463.0 Td (allocate cabin seats, issue live tickets with PNRs, execute check-in baggage weighing with automated excess fee) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 54 449.5 Td (calculation, and perform safe deletions across the entire flight management domain.) Tj ET
Q
q 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 54 432.0 Td (The database was populated with a complete dataset covering 10 international airport hubs, 4 commercial aircraft) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 54 418.5 Td (models, 15 scheduled flight routes, 60 passengers, 60 confirmed bookings, 60 issued e-tickets, and live payment) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 54 405.0 Td (records. A comprehensive battery of analytical SQL queries was executed to validate fleet load factors, route revenue) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 54 391.5 Td (yields, corridor demand, and passenger baggage distribution.) Tj ET
Q
q 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 54 374.0 Td (Functional testing, including live transactional CRUD demonstrations, constraint defense evaluations, and negative) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 54 360.5 Td (testing scenarios, confirmed the absolute correctness of multi-table commits and the structural integrity of the) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 54 347.0 Td (underlying relational schema.) Tj ET
Q
q
