q 0.1 0.2 0.4 rg
BT /F2 14 Tf 54 736 Td (2. PROBLEM STATEMENT) Tj ET
Q
q 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 54 718 Td (Commercial airline operations involve coordinating an enormous volume of interdependent operational and commercial) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 54 704.5 Td (information - passenger credentials, aircraft seating configurations, scheduled flight trajectories, ticket issuance,) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 54 691.0 Td (payment settlements, airport boarding pass generation, baggage weight custody, and cancellation refunds. When such) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 54 677.5 Td (information is managed through manual spreadsheets or un-normalized file systems, several critical failure modes) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 54 664.0 Td (emerge:) Tj ET
Q
q 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 58 646.5 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 70 646.5 Td (Concurrency Contention & Double-Booking: Simultaneous reservation requests attempting to book the same) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 70 633.0 Td (physical seat on the same flight leg result in double-allocation when proper composite unique constraints are) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 70 619.5 Td (absent.) Tj ET
Q
q 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 58 604.0 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 70 604.0 Td (Data Redundancy & Update Anomalies: Repeating aircraft specifications, route distances, and passenger contact) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 70 590.5 Td (details across multiple booking sheets leads to severe relational inconsistencies when changes occur.) Tj ET
Q
q 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 58 575.0 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 70 575.0 Td (Referential Integrity Violations: Deleting a flight or passenger record without foreign-key cascade/restrict protection) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 70 561.5 Td (leaves orphaned tickets, check-in records, and baggage manifests.) Tj ET
Q
q 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 58 546.0 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 70 546.0 Td (Absence of Domain Invariants: Without engine-level CHECK constraints, invalid data - such as negative baggage) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 70 532.5 Td (masses, origin airports identical to destination airports, or departure timestamps succeeding arrival timestamps -) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 70 519.0 Td (enters the database unchecked.) Tj ET
Q
q 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 58 503.5 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 70 503.5 Td (Inefficient Airport Departure Processing: Airport ground staff cannot quickly verify passenger check-in status,) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 70 490.0 Td (calculate excess baggage surcharges accurately \(>15 kg allowance\), or allocate boarding passes in real time.) Tj ET
Q
q 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 58 474.5 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 70 474.5 Td (Lack of Centralized Reporting: Operational questions - such as fleet load factors, route profitability, corridor) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 70 461.0 Td (passenger volume, and cancellation penalty audits - require hours of manual cross-referencing rather than instant) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 70 447.5 Td (SQL aggregation.) Tj ET
Q
q 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 58 432.0 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 70 432.0 Td (Lack of Secure Non-Technical Interface: Administrative staff and ground personnel cannot safely view, search,) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 70 418.5 Td (insert, or delete records without direct, error-prone command-line database access.) Tj ET
Q
q 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 54 403.0 Td (These systemic deficiencies establish the definitive requirement for a normalized, centralized relational database) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 54 389.5 Td (management system accessible through an intuitive, real-time web operations interface - the core objective of this) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 54 376.0 Td (project.) Tj ET
Q
