BT /F2 9.5 Tf 58 497.5 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 70 497.5 Td (First Normal Form \(1NF\): All attributes store atomic, indivisible values. Multi-valued elements \(e.g. passenger bags,) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 70 484.0 Td (multiple tickets under a PNR\) are decomposed into independent child tables with surrogate primary keys.) Tj ET
Q
q 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 58 468.5 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 70 468.5 Td (Second Normal Form \(2NF\): Every table relies on a single-column primary key or full functional dependency. In) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 70 455.0 Td (composite entities, non-key attributes depend on the entire candidate key, eliminating partial dependencies.) Tj ET
Q
q 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 58 439.5 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 70 439.5 Td (Third Normal Form \(3NF\): Non-key attributes depend strictly and exclusively on the primary key, eliminating) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 70 426.0 Td (transitive dependencies. For example, aircraft model and total capacity are stored only in aircraft; flights stores only) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 70 412.5 Td (an aircraft_id foreign key reference rather than duplicating airframe specs.) Tj ET
